# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
"""rpi-audiod: keeps the gadget fed and bridges USB audio and MIDI devices to it (docs/PLAN.md).

While the host streams both ways, it runs jackd on the gadget (mode A) and, for every USB
audio card, a zita-a2j / zita-j2a bridge per direction, connected to that device's gadget
channels. In hub mode the gadget itself is bridged the same way, or by rpi-audio-hostbridge
([usb] host_bridge = "native": lower latency, bridge/audio/hostbridge.c). While the host only
records from the Pi, it plays silence instead: some hosts drop the gadget when nothing plays
into it (docs/hw/2026-10-29-f1-force.md). When the gadget has USB MIDI ports, every MIDI port
of a USB device gets one of them, and the control port takes the commands below from the host too (docs/MIDI.md).

With [engine] mode = "standalone" there is no host: jackd drives a local card (a pHAT DAC, [standalone] in
the settings) from the start, the bridges run as soon as it is up, and the card is one more destination for
the device-to-device routes (docs/MIDI.md). The gadget and its slots are not touched (docs/STANDALONE.md).

  rpi-audiod [run]                            the service (rpi-audiod.service)
  rpi-audiod status                           what the service is doing
  rpi-audiod doctor                           check the installation and the Pi's state
  rpi-audiod --version
  rpi-audiod assign IDENTITY [--in N] [--out N] [--midi K]   pin a device's gadget channels or MIDI port
  rpi-audiod mute IDENTITY in|out on|off      cut or restore a device's audio routes
  rpi-audiod volume IDENTITY in|out PERCENT   set a device's own capture or playback level
  rpi-audiod name IDENTITY [TEXT...]          name a device (empty: clear it)
  rpi-audiod name IDENTITY in|out K [TEXT...] name its channel K (a device name cannot start with "in N" or "out N")
  rpi-audiod route SRC DST [--src P] [--dst P]  play what SRC captures into DST (stereo pair P of each, 1 by default)
  rpi-audiod unroute SRC DST [--src P] [--dst P]  remove it (no pair: every route between them)
  rpi-audiod midiroute SRC DST                send what SRC's MIDI port sends into DST's (IDENTITY or IDENTITY/PORT)
  rpi-audiod midiunroute SRC DST              remove it (an end without a port is any of its ports)
  rpi-audiod cmd TEXT...                      any command above as one text, as the display service sends it
  rpi-audiod preset save N [TEXT...]          save the routing state as preset N (1..8)
  rpi-audiod preset load N | clear N          restore or delete it; Program Change 0..7 on the control
                                              channel loads presets 1..8

Gadget channels are sticky per device identity (/var/lib/rpi-audio/slots.json, which also holds
the names); presets are in presets.json next to it. A full-speed
device is only bridged while its isochronous load fits [usb] fs_budget on its bus. Settings:
/etc/rpi-audio/rpi-audio.toml, then /etc/rpi-audio/rpi-audio.d/*.toml; optional per-device
profiles in /etc/rpi-audio/devices.d/*.toml (config/devices.d/); the gadget's own
come from the GADGET_* environment, or from gadget.env.
"""

